<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo 1996 maize crop around 5.3 mln T-stats office.</title>
<headline>Yugo 1996 maize crop around 5.3 mln T-stats office.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslavia's 1996 maize output stood at around 5.3 million tonnes, a drop of eight percent from last year, the Federal Statistics Office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to the office's preliminary data, average yield on the 1.4 million hectares harvested dropped to 3.72 tonnes per hectare from 4.15 tonnes in 1995, primarily due to a long summer drought.</p>
<p>Yugoslavia last year harvested around 5.7 million tonnes of maize.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
